    "reason": "Full manual annotation was scoped to the primary dataset only. SciFact-Open is covered by the automatic signals above, which are proxies rather than taxonomy labels.",
    "what_cannot_be_claimed": "Because manual taxonomy annotation was carried out on SciFact only, it CANNOT be established which manual failure category becomes dominant on SciFact-Open. The answerable question is narrower than the original Q2 wording: how do comparable AUTOMATIC failure indicators change as the candidate corpus grows roughly 100 times, and how do those shifts relate to the manually observed SciFact taxonomy. A rising gold-missing rate in particular shows that recognised annotated evidence was more often absent; it does NOT establish that the retrieved documents were topically irrelevant, since they may be relevant but non-gold, partially evidential, contradictory, or insufficient. The irrelevant_retrieval label needs document-level human judgement, which only SciFact received.",
